flowchart TB
    accTitle: ACT-R mechanism as summarized across seven fields
    accDescr: The Fan and Lan ACT-R ledger identifies typed buffers, chunks, and procedural productions as state; production matching and conflict resolution as control; buffer match or module event as trigger; persistent chunks and learned utilities with transient buffers; retrieval or production failures; activation, utility, and procedural learning; and capacity and timing constraints.

    S[S: Typed buffers, chunks, procedural productions]
    C[C: Production matching and conflict resolution]
    T[T: Buffer match or module event]
    P[P: Chunks and learned utilities persist; buffers are transient]
    F[F: Retrieval failure, unavailable buffer, no applicable production]
    L[L: Activation and utility updates; procedural learning]
    R[R: Buffer capacity, module timing, central production bottleneck]

    S --> C
    T --> C
    C --> P
    C --> F
    C --> L
    R -. constrains .-> C

    classDef state fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.3px;
    classDef field fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.1px;
    classDef learning fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.2px;
    class S,T state;
    class C,P,F,R field;
    class L learning;
